  "body": "**What.** Guard the certificate centres in code. `lemma6_jump_M.py` refuses a box file without an `x` key, or reads `p` explicitly, instead of falling back silently to `FPM.ZEROS[M]`. Its `inside` check compares against the box's own centre. The 6b\u2081 covering check (C1) compares `ray.json`'s centre with p\u0302. Recommended by #39.\n\n**Why.** The silent fallback put lemma 6a(5)'s run on x\u0302 instead of p\u0302 (#39, #184), and it made the `inside` check vacuous.\n\n**Acceptance (can fail).** I103's box file, which has no `x`, is refused. The covering check fails on a copy of `ray.json` whose `x` differs in the last digit. The M = 3 run's file, which has `x = p^`, is accepted unchanged.\n\n**Depends on.** Nothing.\n",
  "closed_by": null,
